Amazon Simple Storage Service User Guide Working with Amazon S3 Files Topics • What is S3 Files? • How does S3 Files work? • Are you a ﬁrst-time user of S3 Files? • Key concepts • Features • How are you billed for S3 Files? • Prerequisites for S3 Files • Tutorial: Getting started with S3 Files • Mounting your S3 buckets on compute resources • Creating and managing S3 Files resources • Understanding how synchronization works • Monitoring and auditing S3 Files • Performance speciﬁcations • Security for S3 Files • How S3 Files is metered • S3 Files best practices • Unsupported features, limits, and quotas • Troubleshooting S3 Files What is S3 Files? S3 Files is a shared ﬁle system that connects any AWS compute resource directly with your data in Amazon S3. It provides fast, direct access to all of your S3 data as ﬁles with full ﬁle system semantics and low-latency performance, without your data ever leaving S3. Every ﬁle-based application, agent, and team can access and work with your S3 data as a ﬁle system using the tools they already depend on. Built using Amazon EFS, S3 Files gives you the performance and simplicity of a ﬁle system with the scalability, durability, and cost-eﬀectiveness of S3. You can read, write, What is S3 Files? API Version 2006-03-01 1521

